    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-34276",
      "knowledge_point_id": "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction",
      "problem": "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.",
      "worked_solution": "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.",
