      "reasoning": "Every selected answer agrees with its own captured final solution. No grading evidence is supplied. Two source defects remain: q-105261 labels a row scaling as -1/2 although its displayed result requires +1/2; q-127043 has two mathematically correct radio choices, options 1 and 2, because opposite nonzero vectors are both parallel to the line. Its worked solution explicitly supports option 1. Independently, q-34218 has the unique decomposition b=2a1+4a2-2a3, giving product -16. In q-74558, every vector in the span has equal first and third coordinates, requiring k=0; coefficients (2,1) establish sufficiency. In q-74560, every vector in the span has third coordinate twice its first, requiring k=-24; coefficients (-2,-2) establish sufficiency. In q-105248, the first and third equations force s=1,t=-1, but these give second coordinate 6 rather than 5, so u is outside the plane. In q-105261, u=-b-2c gives st=2. The selected vectors in q-34142 and q-105291 are respectively -3a1 and a1/3. In q-34276, a3=a1-a2 proves dependence, so only III is true. In q-105315, determinant -6 proves independence, so II and III are true. Separating constants and coefficients of t gives the vector equations in q-36023 and q-127002. The coefficients of t give parallel vectors in q-32785 and q-127043. For q-32817, the image shows P=(-1,3,2) and Q=(2,4,5); Q-P=(3,1,3), giving the selected parametric equations. Earlier answers for recurring questions remain valid; q-32817 now uses the current escaped-brace choice value. None of the final source answers is mathematically wrong.",
